&Q000407 = A praise poem of Šulgi (Šulgi O)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.4.2.15
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.4.2.15&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div segment A

A.1. iri mu-bi-gin₇ me-a tum₂-ma
#lem: iri[city]; mu[name]; me[Being]; tum[suitable]
#tr.en: City worthy of the divine powers, according to its name: shrine @wSN{Urim}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue in the Louvre, 0.2.02, line 62

A.2. eš₃ urim₂{ki} ud huš ki-en-gi-ra me₃ ki us₂-sa
#lem: eš[shrine]; Urim[1]SN; ud[storm]; huš[reddish]; Kengir[1]; me[battle]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: raging storm of @wGN{Sumer}, battleground -- and well established! Origin of human seed, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. numun i-i suhuš kalam-ma gen₆-ne₂ he₂-ŋal₂ ki us₂-sa
#lem: numun[seed]; e[bring out]; suhuš[foundation]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; gin[confirm]; heŋal[plenty]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: consolidating the foundations of the Land, abundance -- and well established! Lofty dais of @wDN{An}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

A.4. barag mah an-na ki kug ki sikil
#lem: barag[sanctum]; mah[great]; An[1]DN; ki[place]; kug[purify]; ki[place]; sikil[purify]
#tr.en: pure place, holy place, provider of first-fruit offerings for @wDN{An} to refresh himself, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.4

A.5. niŋ₂-saŋ gu₇ an-ne₂ ni₂ te-en-ten lal₃ ŋeštin biz-biz-ze₂-da ki us₂-sa
#lem: nesaŋ[first-fruit offering]; gu[eat]; An[1]DN; ni[self]; ten[extinguish]; lal[syrup]; ŋeštin[vine]; biz[trickle]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: dripping with syrup and wine -- and well established! @wTN{Du-ur}, celebrated place of @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.5

A.6. du₆-ur₂ ki mu tuku {d}en-lil₂-la₂ šag₄-bi me hal-ha
#lem: Duʾur[1]TN; ki[place]; mu[name]; tuku[acquire]; Enlil[1]DN; šag[heart]; me[Being]; hal[divide]
#tr.en: in whose interior are the assigned divine powers, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.6

A.7. ki nam tar-ra a-a {d}en-lil₂-la₂ barag gal ki us₂-sa
#lem: ki[place]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]; aya[father]; Enlil[1]DN; barag[sanctum]; gal[big]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: place whose destiny was decreed by Father @wDN{Enlil}, great dais -- and well established! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.7

A.8. eridug{ki} eš₃ kug-zu nam tar-ra me nun me sikil-la ki us₂-sa
#lem: Eridug[1]SN; eš[shrine]; kugzu[wise]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]; me[Being]; nun[prince]; me[Being]; sikil[pure]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: @wSN{Eridug}, shrine expert in decreeing the fates, with princely divine powers, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.8

A.9. e₂-kiš-nu-ŋal₂-la tur₃ {d}suen-na
#lem: Ekišnuŋal[1]TN; tur[animal stall]; Suen[1]DN
#tr.en: pure divine powers -- and well established! @wTN{E-kiš-nu-ŋal}, cattle-pen of @wDN{Suen}, where fecund cows, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.9

A.10. ab₂ zid {gud}ninda₂ amar kug-ge a-ne di i₃ dug₃-ga ki us₂-sa
#lem: ab[cow]; zid[right]; ninda[breeding bull]; amar[calf]; kug[pure]; ene[pleasure?]; di[speak]; i[oil]; dug[good]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: breed-bulls and holy calves gambol together, producing fine cream -- and well established! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.10

A.11. abzu ki-tuš kug šul {d}suen-na
#lem: abzu[(cosmic) underground water]; kituš[dwelling place]; kug[purify]; šul[youth]; Suen[1]DN
#tr.en: @fsux{Abzu}, holy residence of youthful @wDN{Suen}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.11

A.12. {ŋiš}ešgiri₂ mah an-na saŋ il₂-la u₆ di ki us₂-sa
#lem: ešgiri[staff]; mah[great]; an[sky]; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; u[admiration]; di[speak]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: tall crook lifting its head towards heaven, a marvel -- and well established! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.12

A.13. ŋi₆-par₄ eš₃ nam-hi-li du₃-a me zid nam-en-na ki us₂-sa
#lem: ŋipar[cloister]; eš[shrine]; namhili[charm]; du[build]; me[Being]; zid[right]; namen[the office of en-priest]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: @fsux{Ŋipar}, shrine built in exuberance, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.13

A.14. en nun-na mu gal-zu sikil-la-am₃
#lem: en[priest]; nun[prince]; mu[name]; gal[big]; sikil[pure]
#tr.en: with the true divine powers of the rank of @fsux{en} priestess -- and well established! Princely (?) @fsux{en} priestess, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.14

A.15. suh bur₂-bur₂ {d}nanna ki-tuš dug₃-ge inim dug₃ niŋ₂-si-sa₂-e ki us₂-sa
#lem: suh[crown]; bur[spread out]; Nanna[1]DN; kituš[dwelling place]; dug[good]; inim[word]; dug[good]; niŋsisa[justice]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: your great name is pure; loosener of the headdress of @wDN{Nanna} who makes the dwelling pleasant, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.15

A.16. id₂-nun-kug a zal-le gal-gal-la kun-zu-še₃ ku₆ mušen ki us₂-sa
#lem: Idnunkug[1]WN; a[water]; zal[pass time]; gal[big]; kun[tail]; kud[fish]; mušen[bird]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: with good words and justice -- and well established! @wWN{Id-nun-kug} @noteref{Holy princely river} with ample flowing waters, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.16

A.17. bad₃ niŋin₂-na iri ki ŋa₂-ra-bi šita₂ {ŋiš}tukul ki us₂-sa
#lem: bad[wall]; niŋin[encircle]; iri[city]; ki[place]; ŋar[put]; šita[weapon]; tukul[weapon]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: your reservoir abounds with fish and birds -- and well established! Its city, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.17

A.18. unken ŋar-ra uŋ₃ ša-ra-ba {kuš}gur₂₁!(TUM){ur₃} ki us₂-sa
#lem: unkin[assembly]; ŋar[put]; uŋ[people]; ba[allot]; guru[shield]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: established within the encircling walls, is a battle-mace, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.18

A.19. ki-en-gi-ir-a ki-tuš ŋa₂-ra-bi ni₂ gal ki us₂-sa
#lem: Kengir[1]; kituš[dwelling place]; ŋar[put]; ni[fear]; gal[big]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: a weapon -- and well established! The convened assembly of its numerous people is a shield -- and well established! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.19

A.20. kur-kur ab₂ zid-gin₇ lu-lu-a-bi
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; ab[cow]; zid[right]; lu[abundant]
#tr.en: Great awe of the occupied settlements of @wGN{Sumer} -- and well established! Its foreign lands, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.20

A.21. ab₂ dugud-da u₈ sila₄-da šar₂-ra amaš-a ki us₂-sa
#lem: ab[cow]; dugud[heavy]; u[sheep]; sila[lamb]; šar[numerous]V/i; amaš[sheepfold]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: teeming like herds of fecund cows, fat cows, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.21

A.22. erin₂-bi me₃-še₃ zig₃-ga-bi
#lem: erin[people]; me[battle]; zig[rise]
#tr.en: numerous ewes with their lambs in the sheepfold -- and well established! Its army, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.22

A.23. a e₃-a gaba-ri nu-tuku
#lem: a[water]; e[leave]; gabari[equal]; tuku[acquire]
#tr.en: rising to battle, is an irresistible onrush of water, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.23

A.24. ab hu-luh-ha NI-SUM sumur ki us₂-sa
#lem: ab[sea]; huluh[frightened]; X; sumur[angry]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: a fearsome sea, a raging …… -- and well established! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.24

A.25. [nun]-bi ur-saŋ {d}en-lil₂-la₂ piriŋ ne-na zig₃-ga
#lem: nun[prince]; ursaŋ[warrior]; Enlil[1]DN; piriŋ[lion]; ne[strength]; zig[rise]
#tr.en: Its prince, the hero of @wDN{Enlil}, a lion rising up in its strength, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.25

A.26. [piriŋ ban₃]-da! kur-ra guru₅-uš bur₂-bur₂
#lem: piriŋ[lion]; banda[junior]; kur[mountain(s)]; guruš[cvne]; bur[spread out]
#tr.en: a furious lion (?) baring its teeth at the foreign lands, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26

A.27. [X X] am! gal šu! im-gid₂-gid₂-i
#lem: X; X; am[wild bull]; gal[big]; šu[hand]; gid[long]
#tr.en: …… inspects great wild bulls, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.27

A.28. [...] X gu₇-a SIKI-LAM-bi sud-sud
#lem: X; X; gu[eat]; X; sud[distant]
#tr.en: eating ……, extending ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.28

A.29. [sipad šul]-gi dumu {d}nin-sumun₂-ka
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; Šulgir[1]RN; dumu[child]; Ninsumunak[1]DN
#tr.en: Shepherd @wRN{Šulgi}, son of @wDN{Ninsumun}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.29

A.30. [...] UR₃#-ra he₂-du₇-bi
#lem: X; X; hedu[ornament]
#tr.en: ornament of ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.30

A.31. [...] X-ra#-na inim hul-ne-ne-a
#lem: X; X; inim[word]; hulu[bad]
#tr.en: …… in their evil words, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.31

A.32. [ur-saŋ] {[d]}gilgameš₂# AN en kul-ab{ki}-a-ke₄
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; Gilgameš[1]DN; X; en[lord]; Kulaba[1]SN
#tr.en: brought the hero @wDN{Gilgameš}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.32

A.33. [X X] X NA# im-ma-ni-in-kur₉
#lem: X; X; X; X; kur[enter]
#tr.en: the lord of @wSN{Kulaba} into ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.33

A.34. [X X] kur#-kur-ra-ta inim mu-na-ta-an-e₃
#lem: X; X; kur[mountain(s)]; inim[word]; e[leave]
#tr.en: He produced an utterance for him …… from the foreign lands, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.34

A.35. [...] X e₂-gal-la-na-kam
#lem: X; X; egal[palace]
#tr.en: …… of his palace. 
