A.37. KI X GI URU X gi hal-hal-la-gin₇ igi-ni mu-na-an-ŋal₂
#lem: X; X; X; X; X; gi[reed]; hal[divide]; igi[eye]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#tr.en: …… he looked at him as if on split reeds. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.37

A.38. ud-bi nam kalam-ma ba-tar-ra-ta
#lem: ud[sun]; nam[fate]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; tar[cut]
#tr.en: On the day when the destiny of the Land was determined, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.38

A.39. numun niŋ₂-zi-ŋal₂-la ba-i-a-ta
#lem: numun[seed]; niŋziŋal[living creature]; e[bring out]
#tr.en: when the seed of all living beings was originally brought forth, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.39

A.40. lugal-e {lu₂}tab-ba-ni-ir dalla mu-na-an-e₃-a
#lem: lugal[king]; taba[companion]; dalla[(to be) bright]; e[leave]
#tr.en: when the king appeared radiantly to his comrade -- on that day, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.40

A.41. ud-ba {d}gilgameš₂ en kul-ab{ki}-a-ke₄
#lem: ud[sun]; Gilgameš[1]DN; en[lord]; Kulaba[1]SN
#tr.en: @wDN{Gilgameš}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.41

A.42. šul-gi sipad zid ki-en-gi-ra-ke₄
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; sipad[shepherd]; zid[right]; Kengir[1]
#tr.en: the lord of @wSN{Kulaba}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.42

A.43. ŋiri₃-babbar-ra-na inim mu-ti-ni-ib-e₃
#lem: ŋiribabbara[dawn]; inim[word]; e[leave]
#tr.en: conversed with @wRN{Šulgi}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.43

A.44. ud ul-le₂-aš a-ar-bi ak-de₃
#lem: ud[sun]; ul[distant time]; ar[celebrate]; ak[do]
#tr.en: the good shepherd of @wGN{Sumer}, at his shining feet. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.44

A.45. ud su₃-ra₂-aš šu-a bal-e-de₃
#lem: ud[sun]; sud[distant]; šu[hand]; bala[turn]
#tr.en: So that their praise would be sung forever, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.45

A.46. mu su₃-ra₂-aš nu-ha-lam-e-de₃
#lem: mu[year]; sud[distant]; halam[forsake]
#tr.en: so that it be would handed down to distant days, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.46

A.47. a-ne-ne nam-ur-saŋ kalag-ga-ba
#lem: anene[they]; namursaŋ[heroism]; kalag[strong]
#tr.en: so that it should be not forgotten in remote years, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.47

A.48. teš₂-bi igi zid-de₃-eš im-e-ne
#lem: teš[unity]; igi[eye]; zid[right]; e[speak]
#tr.en: they looked (?) at each other favourably in their mighty heroism. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.48

